|~ What is declared under `::construct`, the step that puts a
   value under a tag through the tag's constructor, `::T<payload>`: the
   refusals of that step. ~|

:construct/construct
  |~~ The step of a constructor invocation from its record, `:tag` and `:payload`, which reads back as itself. ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:construct/PayloadNotSchemaError
  |~~ A `::construct` is a map of `:tag`, a tag, and `:payload`, a
      step.
      ::link~(::construct | doc)
  ~~|

:construct/PayloadNotSchemaError/refusesATagThatIsAKeyword
  |~~ A `:tag` that is a keyword is refused, `:field` naming it. ~~|
  ::law~(::construct{:tag :Box :payload [1]} !| [type /field] | eq [::construct/PayloadNotSchemaError :tag])

:construct/PayloadNotSchemaError/field
  |~~ The field that does not fit, null when the payload is no map. ~~|
  #[::keyword ::null]

:construct/ReadBackDiffersError
  |~~ The `::construct` prints as text that reads back as another step: a
      payload that opens with a name, a digit or a slash is written
      as a group.
      ::link~(::construct | doc)
  ~~|

:construct/ReadBackDiffersError/refusesAPayloadThatJoinsItsTag
  |~~ A number payload prints joined to its tag, which reads back as another name. ~~|
  ::law~(::construct{:tag ::Box :payload 42} !| [type /printed] | eq [::construct/ReadBackDiffersError "::Box42"])

:construct/ReadBackDiffersError/printed
  |~~ The text the step prints as, which reads back as another step or as none. ~~|
  ::string

:construct/TagNotKindError
  |~~ The tag before a payload addresses a kind, a label, a name declared
      by its page, or a word, whose args it lays itself over, `::vec/take[2]`;
      a tag that addresses a name holding a value of its own names nothing
      to build by.
      ::link~(::construct | doc)
  ~~|

:construct/TagNotKindError/refusesTheTagOfAValue
  |~~ The tag of a name that holds a value builds nothing. ~~|
  ::law~(:limit 5 | ::limit[1] !| [type /tag /actualType] | eq [::construct/TagNotKindError ::limit ::number])

:construct/TagNotKindError/laysAWordsTagOverItsArgs
  |~~ The tag of a word lays itself over its args. ~~|
  ::law~(::vec/take[2] | type | eq ::vec/take)

:construct/TagNotKindError/tag
  |~~ The tag, whose node is neither a label nor a word. ~~|
  ::tag
